/* B2B Growth Marketing Dashboard: data file.
   Everything the dashboard shows comes from this file. index.html only draws it.
   All names, companies and numbers below are fictional sample data. */

/* ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   PUT IN YOUR OWN NUMBERS: change the blocks below, save this file,
   then refresh index.html in your browser.

   MQL_INBOUND / MQL_OUTBOUND  MQLs per month: inbound (they came to you)
                and outbound (you went to them: prospecting, imported lists)
   DAILY        one number per day (Jan 1 → end date) for MQLs, meetings,
                SQLs, pipeline £ and deals. The funnel and KPI tiles are
                summed from here, so every date filter stays exact.
   DEALS        [id, deal name, £ value, date]
   PEOPLE       the names behind each funnel bar (click a bar to see them)
   MB           Money Board rows: MQLs that became SQLs
   TARGETS      monthly goals (MQLs, meetings, SQL %, demos, and the north star:
                pipelinePerMonth = £ pipeline from MQLs per month)
   MONTH_NOTES  one-line story per month (shown on hover)
   P            channel tiles per period: li = Channel 1 (paid media),
                gsc + ai = Channel 2 (search), bc = Channel 3,
                content = Channel 4 downloads (contentMql = how many became MQLs)
   EVENTS       each event: MQLs, meetings, spend, cost-per-meeting cap
   ATTRIB_*     U-shaped attribution points per campaign
   CAMPAIGNS    each campaign with its own metric, goal and channel
                (ch: 1–5, matching the channel cards)
   CARDS        rename, re-source, re-goal or hide any KPI / channel tile
   VERIFIED     the date your channel numbers were last checked
   The "Top 3 insights" are plain HTML in index.html.

   WHERE EACH BLOCK COMES FROM (set up & connect)
   CRM (HubSpot, Salesforce…)  DAILY, PEOPLE, DEALS, MB, MQL_*, EVENTS,
                               CAMPAIGNS, and P.bc / P.content / P.demos
   CRM attribution report      ATTRIB_MQL, ATTRIB_CUST (contact create
                               attribution, U-shaped, grouped by campaign)
   Google Analytics 4          P.<period>.ai   AI-referral sessions
   Google Search Console       P.<period>.gsc  non-branded clicks
   Ad platforms                P.<period>.li   spend, clicks, CPC, leads
   Your plan                   TARGETS, and the goals in CARDS
   Exact export steps for each one: README.md → "Connect your data sources".

   KEEP IT FRESH EVERY MORNING
   1. Open this folder in Claude (desktop app → Code tab, or `claude`).
   2. Say "set up my dashboard". Claude asks for your targets and channels,
      checks which tools are connected to your Claude, and tells you which
      CSV to export for any that aren't.
   3. Say "refresh it every weekday at 7am". Claude schedules the refresh:
      it pulls yesterday's numbers, rebuilds this file, checks it and keeps
      a backup of the old one.
   Or paste this file and your exports into any AI assistant and ask it to
   replace these blocks, keeping exactly the same shape.
   ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

